**🚀 Performance & Scalability** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**

**Use the latched failure flag on the per-row gate. Do not run a full source checkpoint for every row.**

`self.read_error()` delegates to `PagedQueryView::read_error`. In this change, that method now runs `provider.check_snapshot(...)` whenever no error is latched. For the stack, `StackProvider::check_snapshot` calls `generation()` and `page_count()` on every pinned source provider. `logical_rows` calls `read_error()` twice for each candidate row (Line 787 and Line 803). `reifiers` does the same at Line 816. As a result, one scan makes about `2 × candidate rows × sources` provider metadata calls, and each call also takes the view mutex. If a provider's `generation()` reads external storage, a large scan or `canonical_paged_seal` makes provider calls proportional to the row count.

Per-row correctness does not need these calls. Drift detected later still fails the operation, because `operation_status` performs the full checkpoint before publication. `canonical_paged_seal` and `query_fallible_view` both check `operation_status` before they publish. Use the latched check (`self.physical.failed()`, which this PR already makes `pub(super)`) inside the row filters. Keep `read_error()` for point reads and the final checkpoint.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Proposed change</summary>

```diff
             .filter_map(move |(stream, page, row)| {
-                if self.read_error().is_some() || !self.visible(page, row) || !seen.insert(row) {
+                if self.physical.failed() || !self.visible(page, row) || !seen.insert(row) {
                     return None;
                 }
@@
                 let classified = classify_statement(physical, true, original, effective);
-                (self.read_error().is_none() && classified == Some(kind)).then_some(row)
+                (!self.physical.failed() && classified == Some(kind)).then_some(row)
             })
```

Apply the same change in `reifiers` (Line 816).
</details>

